Add `video_dip` to the machine config: SW1-5/6 as a SETTING

The 5150's SW1-5/6 pair tells the BIOS which display is PRIMARY, and it is
independent of what is installed - a machine can hold an MDA and a CGA at once
and the switches still name one of them. Upstream derives those bits from the
card list ("any CGA present -> CGA hires"), so a two-card machine always
reports colour whatever order the cards are in, and a mono-primary two-card
5150 cannot be expressed at all.

os8088 needs it because SPEC.md 39.1's vid_detect reads exactly these bits back
out of int 11h to choose its adapter, and the machine the project is
calibrated against holds a Hercules AND a CGA with the switches set to mono -
so every emulated two-card machine booted the OS on the wrong card. SPEC.md
39.11.1's vid_cga_alias runs ONLY when the mono card is primary, which is why
its bug survived: the direction the emulator could reproduce was the one where
the routine never runs.

  video_dip = "mda" | "cga_lores" | "cga_hires" | "expansion"

Optional; absent means derive it as before, so every existing config is
unaffected.
